    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`), alongside the existing human-readable audit line.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **A monotonic sequence** \u2014 `private static final AtomicInteger OWNER_CREATED_SEQ`, incremented once per emitted event so `seq` increases across all creates for the app's lifetime.\n\n2. **An immutable event record** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent(int seq, Integer ownerId, String customerCode, Integer membershipLevel, String event)`. A record is inherently immutable, and its component order fixes the JSON field order `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event}`. A compact constructor hard-codes `event = \"OWNER_CREATED\"`.\n\n3. **`emitOwnerCreatedEvent(owner)`** \u2014 called right after the existing `AUDIT.info(...)` line. It builds the event and logs its JSON serialization on the same `AUDIT` logger via the Jackson 3 `ObjectMapper` already on the classpath. Output looks like:\n   ```\n   {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n   ```\n\n4. **`primaryIdentifier(owner)`** \u2014 the key design point for the spec's forward-looking requirement. The event's identifier field is sourced through this single helper, which returns `owner.getCustomerCode()` today. When the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, only this one method changes and the event automatically carries the memberId instead.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` test (asserting an AUDIT line contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the customerCode) passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
